2026-09-22T00:04:24.024633Z [] {'source_reference_id': 'GSHS9477', 'source_id': 'buynsw', 'title': 'Provision of Mobile Devices and Accessories', 'source_url': None, 'issuing_agency': 'NSW Department of Customer Service', 'category': 'Request for Tender', 'status': 'open', 'publish_date': '2026-09-17', 'closing_date': '2026-10-15', 'value_amount': None, 'value_currency': None, 'value_notes': 'Fixed Unit Prices for 6-month and 12-month validity periods, with quarterly rebates/credits based on volume tiers. No overall contract value specified.', 'location': 'All regions', 'description': "The NSW Department of Customer Service (DCS) is seeking to establish supply arrangements for mobile devices and accessories. The tender aims to secure competitive and transparent pricing, improve order fulfilment and delivery, enhance customer experience, provide effective warranty and support services, and increase operational efficiency through accurate reporting and cost allocation. The scope includes mobile handsets (e.g., Samsung Galaxy S26 5G, Apple iPhone 17), tablets (e.g., iPad Air 11, Apple iPad Mini), Wi-Fi hotspots (D-Link DWR-933M), and various device accessories. Services required include order fulfilment and delivery, warranty and support for a minimum of 12 months, device enrolment into DCS's Apple Business Manager (ABM) or Samsung Knox environments, and delivery to nominated locations at no additional cost. Additional services sought are electronic billing, e-Waste management, and device buy-back services. Telecommunications carrier services, MDM administration beyond ABM/Knox enrolment, end-user technical support, and non-mobile ICT equipment are out of scope.\n\nKey dates for this Request for Tender (RFT) include an issue date of Thursday, September 17, 2026, and a closing date of Thursday, October 15, 2026, at 3:00 PM AEST/AEDT. The last date for clarification questions is Friday, September 25, 2026, at 5:00 PM AEST/AEDT. The estimated contract award date is early February 2027, with a proposed initial contract term from February 2, 2027, to February 1, 2029, and options for up to two additional years. Tender offers must remain valid for six months from the closing time.\n\nMandatory requirements for tenderers include prequalification under the ICT Services Scheme (SCM0020)/Category G01 ? Mobile Devices including Delivery as a Service (or evidence of application), submission of a compliant Modern Slavery Tender Schedule, acknowledgement and annual commitment to the NSW Government Supplier Code of Conduct, disclosure of any conflicts of interest, and a financial viability declaration. Tenderers must also confirm acceptance of the ICT Agreement (ICTA) or clearly identify all proposed departures. Pricing will account for 60% of the total evaluation score, with non-price criteria making up the remaining 40%. An addendum was issued on September 22, 2026, to provide a revised pricing response template.", 'summary_headline': 'NSW Department of Customer Service seeks suppliers for mobile devices and accessories.', 'contact_name': 'Shahana Ferdous', 'contact_email': 'Shahana.Ferdous@customerservice.nsw.gov.au', 'contact_phone': None, 'lodgment_address': 'electronically on the Transaction Platform', 'documents': [{'file_name': 'GSHS9477--Part-A-Request-for-Tender-Conditions.pdf.txt', 'extracted_text': ' \n  Version: 1.0 \n \nDate: October 2024 \n \n \n \nRequest for tender \nPart A - Conditions of Tendering \nRFT Title:  \n \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories \nRFT Number: \n \nGSHS/9477 \n \nRFT issue date: \n \nThursday, 17 September 2026 \nRFT closing date: \n \nThursday, 15 October 2026 \nRFT closing time: \n \n3pm AEST and/or AEDT \nQuotation validity period: \n6 months \nContact officer: \n \nShahana Ferdous \nContact officer?s email: \nShahana.Ferdous@customerservice.nsw.gov.au \nPrequalification Scheme: \nICT Services Scheme (SCM0020)/Category G01 ? Mobile Devices \nincluding Delivery as a Service \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n2 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \nContents \nPart 1 - Invitation to Tender ................................................................................................... 4 \n1. \nInvitation to tender ................................................................................................ 4 \n1.1 \nGeneral .................................................................................................. 4 \n1.2 \nInvitation ................................................................................................ 4 \n1.3 \nIntroduction to Project and its objectives ............................................... 4 \n1.4 \nTenderer registration on Transaction Platform ...................................... 4 \n1.5 \nICT services ........................................................................................... 4 \n1.6 \nProcess and Confidentiality Deed Poll .................................................. 4 \n1.7 \nRFT enquiries ........................................................................................ 5 \n1.8 \nProbity Advisor ....................................................................................... 5 \n1.9 \nValue for money..................................................................................... 5 \nPart 2 - Conditions of Tendering ........................................................................................... 6 \n2. \nTender documents ................................................................................................ 6 \n2.1 \nTender Documents comprise ................................................................ 6 \n2.2 \nOwnership of Tender Documents and confidentiality ............................ 6 \n2.3 \nInconsistency ......................................................................................... 6 \n2.4 \nClarification and amendment of Tender Documents ............................. 6 \n2.5 \nPrincipal not bound by oral information ................................................. 7 \n2.6 \nReturn or destruction of Tender Documents ......................................... 7 \n2.7 \nPrivacy ................................................................................................... 7 \n3. \nTenderer to fully inform itself .............................................................................. 8 \n3.1 \nTenderer to do ....................................................................................... 8 \n3.2 \nPre-tender briefing and other key dates ................................................ 8 \n3.3 \nInteractive Process ................................................................................ 9 \n3.4 \nPolicies, Codes and Standards ............................................................. 9 \n3.5 \nAccepted standards of behaviour ........................................................ 11 \n4. \nLodgement of tender .......................................................................................... 12 \n4.1 \nRequirement to lodge .......................................................................... 12 \n4.2 \nElectronic Tender submission ............................................................. 12 \n4.3 \nAcceptance of Conditions of Tendering .............................................. 13 \n4.4 \nFormat ................................................................................................. 13 \n4.5 \nCompleted Tender Form ..................................................................... 13 \n4.6 \nCompleted Tender Schedules ............................................................. 13 \n4.7 \nEvidence of agent?s authority .............................................................. 14 \n4.8 \nAcceptable legal entities ...................................................................... 14 \n4.9 \nTender prices ....................................................................................... 14 \n4.10 \nOwnership of Tenders ......................................................................... 14 \n5. \nTender validity period ......................................................................................... 15 \n6. \nVariations, non-conforming tenders and alternative tenders ........................ 15 \n6.1 \nVariations to Tenders .......................................................................... 15 \n6.2 \nRejection of Non-Conforming Tenders ................................................ 15 \n6.3 \nAlternative Tenders ............................................................................. 16 \n7. \nTender evaluation ............................................................................................... 16 \n7.1 \nAcknowledgement of receipt of Tender ............................................... 16 \n7.2 \nInformation requests ............................................................................ 16 \n7.3 \nEvaluation ............................................................................................ 16 \n7.4 \nEvaluation criteria ................................................................................ 17 \n7.5 \nDisclosure of Tender information ......................................................... 17 \n7.6 \nExchange of information between Authorities ..................................... 17 \n7.7 \nDue diligence ....................................................................................... 18 \n\n \n \n3 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \n8. \nNo contract and no obligation to consider or accept any tender .................. 18 \n8.1 \nNo Contract .......................................................................................... 18 \n8.2 \nNo obligation ........................................................................................ 18 \n8.3 \nThe Principal not liable ........................................................................ 19 \n8.4 \nDiscretions of the Principal .................................................................. 19 \n8.5 \nRe-seller Model.................................................................................... 21 \n9. \nFormal contract required ................................................................................... 21 \n10. \nDisclaimer ............................................................................................................ 22 \n11. \nTenderer?s warranty and acknowledgement .................................................... 22 \n11.1 \nTenderer?s warranty ............................................................................. 22 \n11.2 \nTenderer?s acknowledgement ............................................................. 23 \n12. \nTenderer bears costs .......................................................................................... 23 \n13. \nGoverning law and jurisdiction ......................................................................... 23 \n14. \nComplaints procedure ........................................................................................ 23 \n15. \nDefinitions and interpretation ............................................................................ 24 \n15.1 \nDefinitions ............................................................................................ 24 \n15.2 \nInterpretation ........................................................................................ 27 \nAnnexure A ? Tender Particulars ........................................................................................ 27 \n \n \n\n \n \n4 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \nPart 1 - Invitation to Tender  \n1. \nInvitation to tender \n1.1 \nGeneral \nThe Principal is seeking Tenders from suitably qualified and experienced Tenderers who can \ndemonstrate that they satisfy the Principal\'s requirements as described in this RFT. \n1.2 \nInvitation \nThe Principal invites each Tenderer to submit a conforming tender in accordance with the \nTender Documents for the performance of the Project.  This document is not an offer by the \nPrincipal to enter into any agreement, whether on the terms and conditions set out in the \nConditions of Contract or otherwise, it is a mere invitation to treat. \n1.3 \nIntroduction to Project and its objectives \nThe Principal invites the Tenderer to submit a Tender for the Project. The Tender Particulars \nmay provide further detail in respect of the background of the Project and the Principal?s key \npriorities in relation to the Project.  \n1.4 \nTenderer registration on Transaction Platform  \n(a) \nThe Tenderer acknowledges that:  \n(i) \nthe Principal generally conducts business with tenderers electronically; \nand \n(ii) \nthe Principal uses an electronic platform (the Transaction Platform) as \nthe platform for seeking Tenders from Tenderers. \n(b) \nIn order to conduct business with the Principal, the Tenderer will need to be \nregistered on the Transaction Platform.  \n(c) \nNotices given to a Tenderer whether before or after the Closing Time may be \nposted or transmitted on the Transaction Platform or by email to a Tenderer\'s \naddress for notices given in the Tender Form, and such posting or transmission will \nbe taken to be good service of such notices. \n1.5 \nICT services \nWhere the Tender Particulars specify that this RFT relates to information and communications \ntechnology (ICT) goods or services: the Tenderer warrants that it is registered on (or has \napplied for registration on) the NSW government ICT goods and services prequalification \nscheme, and must provide evidence of such registration as part of its Tender. \nFurther details regarding the scheme can be found at https://buy.nsw.gov.au/ \n1.6 \nProcess and Confidentiality Deed Poll \nThis clause 1.6 applies where the Tender Particulars specify that a Process and Confidentiality \nDeed Poll is required. \nThe Principal will make the remaining Tender Documents available to Tenderers who have \nexecuted and delivered to the Principal the Process and Confidentiality Deed Poll. The \nTenderer acknowledges that certain Tender Documents may (if required by the Principal) be \nmade available to the Tenderer through a data room or equivalent environment. \n\n \n \n5 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \nTenderers who have not provided to the Principal an executed Process and Confidentiality \nDeed Poll will only obtain access to receive the remaining Tender Documents once the \nPrincipal receives the executed Process and Confidentiality Deed Poll, and the Tenderer will \nnot have any entitlement to an extension to the Closing Time. Access to the remaining Tender \nDocuments will be granted to Tenderers only after the Principal receives their executed \nProcess and Confidentiality Deed Poll. No extensions to the Closing Time will be granted to \nTenderers who haven\'t provided this documentation. \n1.7 \nRFT enquiries  \nAll enquiries:  \n(a) \nregarding the RFT (including clarifications and questions regarding the Tender \nDocuments and Information Documents);  \n(b) \nrelating to registration, log-in and profile editing matters; and \n(c) \nrelating to any other matter (including issues with electronic lodgement of Tenders), \nmust be in writing and directed to the Principal?s Contact Person, or as otherwise directed by \nthe Principal, including to buy.nsw@customerservice.nsw.gov.au for enquiries relating to \nregistration, log-in and profile editing matters.  \n1.8 \nProbity Advisor  \n(a) \nThis clause 1.8 applies if stated in the Tender Particulars.  \n(b) \nThe Principal has appointed, or will appoint, a Probity Advisor to monitor this RFT \nprocess and ensure that the process is applied fairly and equitably to all Tenderers. \n(c) \nThe Probity Advisor is an independent observer of the RFT process and may be \npresent at meetings, interviews and workshops during the RFT process. \n(d) \nIf the Tenderer has any concerns about the conduct or probity of the selection \nprocess, the Tenderer should promptly bring its concerns to the Probity Advisor\'s \nattention. \n1.9 \nValue for money \nThe New South Wales Procurement Policy Framework recognises that the overarching \nconsideration for government procurement is ensuring best value for money in the \nprocurement of goods and services. In determining whether a procurement represents value \nfor money, the Principal may consider the financial and non-financial costs and benefits of \nmaking the procurement and the quantity and quality, environmental sustainability and whole-\nof-life costs of the Contractor\'s Activities (among other considerations).  \n\n \n \n6 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \nPart 2 - Conditions of Tendering \n2. \nTender documents \n2.1 \nTender Documents comprise \nThe Tender Documents comprise the following: \n(a) \nThis Part A of this RFT (Conditions of Tendering); \n(b) \nPart B of this RFT (Returnable Schedules) the Statement of Work; and  \n(c) \nPart C the Conditions of Contract (including any Schedules and Annexures). \n2.2 \nOwnership of Tender Documents and confidentiality \n(a) \nThe Tender Documents, and any intellectual property rights in them, are and \nremain the property of the Principal. \n(b) \nThe Tender Documents and the Information Documents are strictly confidential \nwhere identified as such.  A Tenderer must not (and it agrees that it will not) copy, \nuse or disclose the Tender Documents or Information Documents to others except \nfor the purpose of preparing and submitting a Tender.  If a Tenderer does disclose \nany of the Tender Documents or Information Documents to others for that purpose, \nit must only do so on the same basis as is set out in this clause 2.2 and it must \nobtain an undertaking from each such other person in the same terms as this \nclause. \n(c) \nNothing in this clause 2.2 limits the operation of the Process and Confidentiality \nDeed Poll (if any). \n2.3 \nInconsistency \n(a) \nIf there is any inconsistency between this RFT and any other document provided to \nTenderers by the Principal preceding or following the release of this RFT (other \nthan changes made in the form of an Addendum), this RFT will prevail to the extent \nof the inconsistency. \n(b) \nIf a provision of the Conditions of Contract is inconsistent with a provision in this \nRFT, the provision in the Conditions of Contract will prevail. \n2.4 \nClarification and amendment of Tender Documents \n(a) \nIf a Tenderer finds or reasonably believes it has found any discrepancy, error, \nambiguity, inconsistency or omission in this RFT or any other documents given or \nmade available by the Principal in respect of this RFT (including any Addenda \nissued under this clause 2.4), it must immediately submit a written request for \nclarification to the Principal\'s Contact Person. \n(b) \nAt any time prior to the formation of a Contract for the performance of the Project in \nthe manner stated in clause 9, the Principal and/or the Principal\'s Contact Person \nmay (but without being obliged to do so), for any reason, clarify, add to, modify or \notherwise amend the Tender Documents by issuing an Addendum. \n(c) \nEach Addendum will be issued to all Tenderers, except that: \n\n \n \n7 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \n(i) \nwhere, after the Closing Time, some but not all Tenderers are short \nlisted, further Addenda may only be sent to the short-listed \nTenderers; and \n(ii) \nwhere, after the Closing Time, any preferred Tenderers are identified, \nfurther Addenda might only be sent to the preferred Tenderers. \n(d) \nAn Addendum may include the text of the request for clarification or other question \nor matter which led to the Addendum being issued, but will not identify the Tenderer \nwho sought the clarification or raised the question. \n(e) \nIf requested by the Principal, the Tenderer must promptly acknowledge receipt of all \nAddenda issued to it by notice in writing sent to the Principal\'s Contact Person.  \n2.5 \nPrincipal not bound by oral information \nWithout limiting clause 10, to the extent permitted by Law, the Principal is not bound by, and \nhas no responsibility or liability for, any oral advice, representation or information given or \nfurnished by or on behalf of the Principal or the Principal\'s Contact Person with respect to the \nTender Documents, the Project, the Contractor\'s Activities, the tender process, any Information \nDocument, any Tender or any Contract, whether given or made before or after the Closing \nTime. \n2.6 \nReturn or destruction of Tender Documents \nEach Tenderer who does not intend to submit a Tender, or whose Tender is unsuccessful, \nmust within 14 days of:  \n(a) \nreceiving the Tender Documents; or  \n(b) \nbeing advised that it has been unsuccessful, \n(as the case may be), if requested by the Principal\'s Contact Person, either: \n(c) \nsecurely return all Tender Documents and Information Documents (including all \ncopies) to the Principal to a place directed by the Principal and provide evidence to \nthe Principal\'s complete satisfaction that all electronic versions have been \npermanently erased from all computers and other means of storage; or \n(d) \ndemonstrate to the complete satisfaction of the Principal that all Tender Documents \nand Information Documents (including all copies) have been securely and \npermanently destroyed and that all electronic versions have been completely and \npermanently erased from all computers and other means of storage. \n2.7 \nPrivacy \nTenderers must provide a copy of the following statement to all individuals named in, or whose \npersonal information is provided to the Principal as part of, its Tender:  \nPersonal information about you may have been provided to and collected by the \nDepartment of Customer Service as part of a Tender.  The Department of Customer \nService is committed to protecting privacy in accordance with all relevant privacy \nlaws, including its obligations under the Privacy and Personal Information \nProtection Act 1998 (NSW).  The Department of Customer Service intends to use \npersonal information that it obtains in connection with a Tender to evaluate the \nTender as well as contract assessment and management.  The Department of \nCustomer Service may disclose the personal information provided in connection \nwith the Tender to other government departments and agencies.  You are entitled \naccess to the personal information the Department of Customer Service has \n\n \n \n8 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \ncollected about you, subject to legislative exceptions.  By providing any personal \ninformation in connection with the Tender or being named in this Tender, you agree \nthat the Department of Customer Service may collect, use and disclose such \npersonal information for the purposes described above. \nIf you have any enquiries about your personal information, you may contact the \nDepartment of Customer Service at privacy@customerservice.nsw.gov.au. \n3. \nTenderer to fully inform itself \n3.1 \nTenderer to do \nWithout in any way limiting what a Tenderer does, a Tenderer must do all of the following prior \nto submitting its Tender: \n(a) \nexamine and carefully check and acquire actual knowledge of the contents of all of \nthe Tender Documents; \n(b) \ninform itself completely as to:  \n(i) \nthe risks, contingencies and other circumstances which might have an \neffect on the execution of the Project or the cost of executing the Project; \n(ii) \nthe nature of the work and of the resources, plant, equipment, materials \nand other items necessary for the execution of the Project; \n(iii) \nthe availability and cost of resources, labour, plant, equipment, materials \nand other items required (including all relevant industrial conditions); \n(iv) \nall applicable Law, taxes, duties, levies, charges, fees and insurance \npremiums (including compulsory insurance premiums); and \n(v) \nall Authority requirements relating to the Contract and the Project;  \n(c) \nprepare its Tender based on its own investigations, interpretations, deductions, \ninformation and determinations; \n(d) \nmake its own enquiries to determine the adequacy, accuracy, suitability and \ncompleteness of any Information Document; \n(e) \nsatisfy itself as to the correctness and sufficiency of its Tender and that the rates \nand prices offered in its Tender cover the cost of complying with all of its obligations \nunder the Contract and of all matters and inputs necessary for the due and proper \nperformance and completion of its obligations under the Contract; and \n(f) \nobtain all appropriate professional, commercial and technical advice with respect to \nthe matters referred to in clauses 3.1(a) to (e), \nand any failure by the Tenderer to do any of those things will not relieve the Tenderer of its \nobligation to perform and complete the Project and the Contractor\'s Activities in accordance \nwith the Contract should the Contract be awarded to it or entitle the Tenderer to make any \nClaim. \n3.2 \nPre-tender briefing and other key dates \nWhere specified in the Tender Particulars, Tenderers are invited to attend a pre-tender briefing \nat the time specified in the Tender Particulars.  \n\n \n \n9 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \nOther key dates (if any) are set out in the Tender Particulars. Any such dates are indicative \nonly and are subject to change. \n3.3 \nInteractive Process \n(a) \nEither or both the Principal and the Principal\'s Contact Person may, in their \ndiscretion, interview, meet with or hold workshops with any one or more of the \nTenderers (Interactive Process). \n(b) \nIf a Tenderer is called to such an Interactive Process, the Tenderer must be \nrepresented by an authorised person (or persons) of its Personnel who have the \nnecessary knowledge and expertise, and who are familiar with all technical, financial \nand contractual details of the Tender. \n(c) \nThe Principal may provide a protocol for the Interactive Process, and the Tenderer \nand its Personnel must comply with such protocol. \n(d) \nDuring the Interactive Process:  \n(i) \nthe Principal may (in its absolute discretion) choose to identify aspects of \nany proposed Tender that are deficient. However, the Principal will not \nbe obliged to identify issues or otherwise conduct the Interactive Process \nwith the various Tenderers in the same way, to the same extent or as to \nthe same subject matter; and \n(ii) \nthe Principal\'s silence in respect of any aspect of a Tenderer?s \nsubmission or any other issue raised will not constitute endorsement or \napproval of any aspect of a Tender. \n(e) \nTenderers acknowledge and agree that: \n(i) \nneither the Principal nor the Tenderer intends to create any contract or \nother relationship under which the Principal is legally obliged to conduct \nany Interactive Process in any manner at all and that there is in fact no \nsuch contract or other relationship in existence; \n(ii) \nthere will be no procedural or substantive limitation upon the manner in \nwhich the Principal may conduct any Interactive Process; \n(iii) \ninformation provided by the Tenderer during the Interactive Process, and \nany materials derived therefrom, will be taken to be part of the Tender;  \n(iv) \nany participation by the Tenderer(s) in any Interactive Process is \nbecause it considers that this represents a valuable commercial \nopportunity for the Tenderer; and \n(v) \nthe Principal is proceeding with any Interactive Process in reliance upon \nthe acknowledgements set out above. \n3.4 \nPolicies, Codes and Standards \n(a) \nTenderers must (and must ensure that each of their Personnel) inform themselves \nof, and comply with:  \n(i) \nthe New South Wales Procurement Policy Framework (including for the \nduration of any Contract), a copy of which is available at \nhttps://buy.nsw.gov.au/; \n\n \n \n10 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \n(ii) \nthe New South Wales Government Supplier Code of Conduct, a copy of \nwhich is available at https://buy.nsw.gov.au/; \n(iii) \nthe Principal\'s Code of Ethics and Conduct, which is available at \nhttps://www.nsw.gov.au/customer-service/who-we-are/code-of-ethics-\nand-\nconduct#:~:text=To%20work%20ethically%20means%20you,of%20work\ning%20to%20your%20colleagues; \n(iv) \nthe Principal\'s Statement of Business Ethics, a copy of which is available \nat https://www.nsw.gov.au/customer-service/who-we-are/business-\nethics-statement;  \n(v) \nthe SME & Regional Procurement Policy (including by submitting a \n"SME and Local Participation Plan" as referred to in the SME & Regional \nProcurement Policy if the Contract is valued at $3 million or more);  \n(vi) \nthe New South Wales Government Aboriginal Procurement Policy, a \ncopy of which is available at https://buy.nsw.gov.au/  including, if the \nContract is valued at $7.5 million or more: \nA. \nby submitting an Aboriginal Participation Plan that sets out \nhow the Tenderer plans to meet the Aboriginal participation \nrequirements; and \nB. \nby declaring whether the Tenderer has previously \nparticipated, or is currently participating, in a New South \nWales government contract that had Aboriginal participation \nrequirements and, if applicable, demonstrating the Tenderer\'s \ncompliance with the requirements;  \n(vii) \nthe Worst Forms of Child Labour Convention,1999 (ILO Convention 182) \nincluding to ensure that the Contractor\'s Activities will not be produced \nusing the "worst forms of child labour" as defined; and \n(viii) \nto the extent applicable, the ICT/Digital SME procurement commitments, \na copy of which is available at \nhttps://buy.nsw.gov.au/resources/ictdigital-sovereign-procurement-\ncommitments;  \n(ix) \nany other NSW government policies, codes or standards referenced in \nthe Contract or the Tender Documents (including those relating to \ninformation security or cyber-security). \n(x) \nPBD 2017-07 Conduct by Suppliers, a copy of which is available at \nhttps://arp.nsw.gov.au/pbd-2017-07-draft-conduct-suppliers. Tenderers \nmust also inform the Principal of any findings of dishonest, unfair, \nunconscionable, corrupt or illegal conduct against the Tenderer, its \ndirectors or its management; and \n(xi) \nif the Contract is valued at $7.5 million or more, the Small Business \nShorter Payment Terms Policy. \n(b) \nTenderers acknowledge that the EPP Direction applies to this RFT if stated in the \nTender Particulars.  \n\n \n \n11 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \n3.5 \nAccepted standards of behaviour \n(a) \nThe Principal expects the highest standards of ethical behaviour from those with \nwhom it contracts and that its vendors will conduct their business relationships in \naccordance with the Law. Findings of dishonest, unfair, unconscionable, corrupt or \notherwise illegal conduct against the Principal\'s vendors can adversely affect the \nreputation of the Principal and the State of New South Wales \n(b) \nTenderers must not engage in collusive behaviour, anti-competitive conduct or any \nsimilar conduct with another Tenderer or any other person in relation to the \nprocurement process. Without limitation, Tenderers must not: \n(i) \nenter into any contract, arrangement or understanding for the purpose of, \nor one of the purposes being that, in the event that the Tenderer is the \npreferred Tenderer, they will pay or provide to any unsuccessful \nTenderer or any other person money or any benefits or fulfil any \nundertaking which is a consequence of any collusive circumstance in \nrelation to a Tender or any contract resulting from the Tender; \n(ii) \nhave any knowledge of the rates or prices of any other Tenderer prior to \nsubmitting its Tender, nor disclose to any competing Tenderer the rates \nor prices in its Tender; or \n(iii) \ndeliberately set the rates and prices in their Tender in order to enhance \nthe price of any other Tenderer\'s Tender.  \n(c) \nTenderers must disclose in their Tender:  \n(i) \nany actual, perceived or potential conflict of interest (whether pecuniary \nor non-pecuniary) in relation to this RFT or the Project; and \n(ii) \nany personal relationships or associations between the Principal and its \nPersonnel and any office holder or senior manager of the Tenderer in its \nTender. \n(d) \nTenderers should note that, among other grounds, a person:  \n(i) \nadversely named by the Independent Commission Against Corruption \n(ICAC); or \n(ii) \nwhose behaviour or actions (regardless of whether or not such is in \nrelation to this RFT), in the Principal\'s opinion, might reflect badly on the \nPrincipal or the State of New South Wales, \nmay, to the extent permitted by Law, be prohibited from performing any work for the \nPrincipal in any capacity including directly as an employee, contractor or \nsubcontractor or as an employee of a contractor or subcontractor.  \n(e) \nTenderers must comply with the Modern Slavery Act 2018 (NSW) and the NSW \nAnti-slavery Commissioner?s Guidance on Reasonable Steps to Manage Modern \nSlavery Risks in Operations and Supply-Chains, including by: \n(i) \ntaking reasonable steps to identify, assess and address Modern Slavery \nin its operations and supply chain and ensure compliance with Modern \nSlavery Laws; and \n(ii) \nagreeing that, if it is the successful Tenderer, it may be required to \ncomply with modern slavery contract clauses in the contract entered into \n\n \n \n12 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \nwith the Principal. For more information visit Modern Slavery and \nProcurement.  \n(f) \nIf any Tenderer fails to comply with the requirements of clause 3.4 or this clause \n3.5, the Principal may take such failure into account when considering the Tender \nsubmitted by a Tenderer, which may result in the Tender being rejected. \n4. \nLodgement of tender \n4.1 \nRequirement to lodge \nThe complete Tender submission must be lodged electronically on the Transaction Platform by \nno later than the Closing Time in accordance with clause 4.2. \n4.2 \nElectronic Tender submission \n(a) \nA Tender must be lodged in accordance with any written instructions provided to \nthe Tenderer by the Principal.  Any Tender that does not comply with the Principal?s \ninstructions for lodgement may, in the Principal\'s absolute discretion, be \ndisregarded and not be considered by the Principal. \n(b) \nTenders must not contain any macros, applets or executable code or executable \nfiles (including files compressed by WinZip or other means), unless expressly \nrequired by this RFT.  Tenderers must ensure that all electronically transmitted files \nare free from viruses by checking the files with an up-to-date virus checking \nprogram before lodgement.   \n(c) \nTender responses must be in a file format that can be read, formatted, displayed \nand printed by currently supported editions of Microsoft Office System?, or Adobe \nAcrobat?, or any other format specified by the Principal. \n(d) \nWhen a Tender is lodged a confirmation e-mail will be sent to the Tenderer\'s e-mail \naddress.  If no acknowledgement has been received, the Tenderer should advise \nthe Principal immediately (contact details set out in Annexure A of this RFT).   \n(e) \nIf a Tenderer has problems accessing the Transaction Platform website or \nelectronically submitting a Tender or has failed to receive a receipt confirming \nreceipt of the Tender: \n(i) \n(e)(i)the Tenderer should inform the Principal\'s Contact Person; and \n(ii) \nif there is a defect or failure of the Transaction Platform and the \nPrincipal\'s Contact Person is notified, the Principal may admit the \nTenderer into consideration, provided that in the view of the Principal, \nthe integrity and competitiveness of the RFT process will not be \ncompromised.  \n(f) \nTo the extent permitted by Law, the Principal accepts no responsibility or liability to \nTenderers in connection with, or arising out of, the electronic transmission of \nTender information, including in relation to security, confidentiality, privacy or data \ncorruption.  Tenderers are responsible for ensuring that they have adequate \nelectronic security systems in place. \n(g) \nA Tender submitted electronically will be treated in accordance with the Electronic \nTransactions Act 2000 (NSW) and given no lesser level of confidentiality, probity \nand attention than Tenders lodged by other means.  \n(h) \nA Tenderer, by electronically lodging a Tender, is taken to have accepted the \nconditions detailed in this RFT and any conditions of the Transaction Platform. \n\n \n \n13 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \n4.3 \nAcceptance of Conditions of Tendering \nBy lodging a Tender, the Tenderer confirms that it is bound by these Conditions of Tendering. \n4.4 \nFormat \n(a) \nThe Tender must be compiled in sections and in the following order: \n(i) \nSection 1 - Completed Tender Form (see clause 4.5); and \n(ii) \nSection 2 - Completed Tender Schedules (see clause 4.6). \n(b) \nThe Tender and all documents forming part of the Tender submission must be in \nEnglish and all measurements and quantities must be in units consistent with the \nprovisions of the National Measurement Act 1960 (Cth) and the International \nSystem of Units. \n4.5 \nCompleted Tender Form \n(a) \nA Tenderer must duly complete and submit the Tender Form included in the Tender \nDocuments. \n(b) \nThe completed Tender Form must be signed by a duly authorised agent of each \nTenderer.   \n(c) \nWhere a Tenderer comprises 2 or more persons (whether a joint venture, \nconsortium, partnership or any other unincorporated grouping of 2 or more \npersons): \n(i) \nthe Tenderer must include in its Tender submission: \nA. \nfor each of the persons who comprise the Tenderer, all of \nthose details about the Tenderer that are required by the \nTender Documents;  \nB. \na copy of the agreement governing the arrangements \nbetween those persons (whether a joint venture agreement, \nconsortium agreement, partnership agreement or otherwise); \nand \nC. \nsuch other information as reasonably requested by the \nPrincipal; and \n(ii) \neach of those persons is jointly and severally bound by the Tender and \nthese Conditions of Tendering. \n4.6 \nCompleted Tender Schedules \n(a) \nTenderers must duly complete and submit all of the Tender Schedules that form \npart of the Tender Documents and provide all other information required by the \nTender Schedules. \n(b) \nTenderers must complete the Tender Schedules without amending the existing text. \n(c) \nAny Tender Schedule which addresses a price issue must be contained in a \nseparate file attachment from the other Tender documents.  Prices should only be \ndisclosed in the Tender Schedule relevant to pricing.  \n\n \n \n14 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \n4.7 \nEvidence of agent?s authority \nIf requested to do so by the Principal\'s Contact Person, a Tenderer must produce evidence of \nthe authority of any agent who has signed any part of the Tender on behalf of the Tenderer. \n4.8 \nAcceptable legal entities \n(a) \nTenderers must be identified by an ABN or ARBN and be registered for GST as \nrequired by Law or any applicable NSW Government procurement scheme rules or \ndirections.  \n(b) \nTo the extent permitted by Law, the Principal will not accept any Tender from an \nentity that is: \n(i) \na corporate entity with persons involved directly or indirectly in the \nmanagement of the entity who are disqualified persons under the \nCorporations Act 2001 (Cth) or by court order; or \n(ii) \nbankrupt or insolvent.  \n(c) \nAny Tender by a joint venture must identify the legal entities that propose to enter \nany Contract. \n(d) \nAny Tender by a trustee must include the trust deed and any other constituent \ndocuments. \n4.9 \nTender prices  \n(a) \nPrices and rates tendered must include all costs of performing the Contract, \nincluding all taxes (other than GST), as well as any fees and charges that the \nTenderer may be liable for.  \n(b) \nTendered prices, fees, rates, charges and any other amounts must be expressed \nexclusive of GST. \n(c) \nWithout limiting clause 5, prices and rates offered by a Tenderer in its Tender are to \nremain fixed and open for acceptance by the Principal for the Tender Validity \nPeriod. \n(d) \nBy submitting a Tender, the Tenderer acknowledges and agrees that if it is awarded \nthe Tender based on the pricing or compensation information it has submitted in its \ntender documents, this submitted pricing or compensation will allow it to perform \nthe contract without causing or contributing to modern slavery, and to provide or \nenable an effective remedy to any modern slavery it does cause or to which it does \ncontribute. \n4.10 \nOwnership of Tenders \n(a) \nUnless otherwise agreed in writing, all Tenders (including any samples) become the \nproperty of the Principal upon lodgement and will not be returned to the Tenderer. \n(b) \nTenderers submit documents in response to this RFT on the basis that the Principal \nmay use, retain and copy the information contained in those documents for the \npurposes of: \n(i) \nevaluating, selecting and preparing any contract with respect to this RFT; \nand \n(ii) \nthe development of any other procurement conducted by the Principal. \n\n \n \n15 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \nIn addition, the Principal may disclose Tender documents or any part of such \nTender documents to third parties for the purposes of assisting the Principal in the \nconduct of the RFT process, including in connection with the Tender evaluation, \nnegotiation and the preparation of any Contract. \n(c) \nNothing in this clause 4.10 changes or affects the ownership of intellectual property \nin the information contained in the Tender documents. \n5. \nTender validity period \n(a) \nOn delivery of a Tender, each Tenderer makes a valid, irrevocable and \nunconditional offer to the Principal to enter into an agreement on the terms and \nconditions set out in the Conditions of Contract, which is open for acceptance by \nthe Principal in its sole discretion, until the end of the Tender Validity Period, \ndespite any selection of preferred Tenderer(s) during the Tender Validity Period. \n(b) \nThe Tenderer agrees that any notice withdrawing or purporting to withdraw a \nTender that is given prior to the expiry of the Tender Validity Period will be \nineffective. \n(c) \nNothing in this clause 5 limits the operation of clause 8.4 in any way. \n6. \nVariations, non-conforming tenders and alternative tenders \n6.1 \nVariations to Tenders \nA Tenderer may replace, amend or supplement its Tender only if invited to do so by the \nPrincipal.  The Principal reserves the right to ask for replacement, amended or supplemental \nTenders from one or more Tenderers but is under no obligation to do so.  The Principal is \nentitled, in its absolute discretion, to consider and accept a replacement, amended or \nsupplemental Tender from any Tenderer (whether requested by the Principal or not) and \nwithout reference to any other Tenderers. The Principal is not required to extend the same \nopportunity to each Tenderer. \n6.2 \nRejection of Non-Conforming Tenders \n(a) \nA Tender: \n(i) \nthat is not lodged by the Closing Time as required by clause 4.1; \n(ii) \nthat does not contain all the documents and other information required \nby the Tender Documents (including these Conditions of Tendering);  \n(iii) \nthat does not comply in every respect with the Conditions of Tendering; \nor \n(iv) \nthat seeks to include a Tenderer\'s own conditions of tendering or \nconditions of contract, \n(Non-Conforming Tender) may be rejected and/or not considered, regardless of \nthe reason for the late lodgement or the non-conformance. \n(b) \nNotwithstanding clause 6.2(a), the Principal is entitled, in its absolute discretion, to \nconsider and accept a Non-Conforming Tender. \n\n \n \n16 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \n6.3 \nAlternative Tenders \n(a) \nA Tenderer may submit one or more Tenders that propose materials, quantities, \nspecifications or methodologies which are different from the solutions, materials, \nquantities, specifications or methodologies specified in this RFT (Alternative \nTender), provided it has also submitted a Tender that complies with the \nrequirements of the Tender Documents.   \n(b) \nAn Alternative Tender must: \n(i) \nmeet the intent and objective of the RFT; \n(ii) \nbe marked ?ALTERNATIVE TENDER? and include relevant Tender \nSchedules;  \n(iii) \ninclude clear and precise details of how and to what extent the \nAlternative Tender varies from the requirements of the RFT and what \nadvantages (including better value for money or other benefits) the \nAlternative Tender offers to the Principal at each divergence from the \nRFT; and \n(iv) \nbe a conforming Tender in all other respects. \n(c) \nThe Principal is entitled, in its absolute discretion, to consider and accept an \nAlternative Tender. \n7. \nTender evaluation \n7.1 \nAcknowledgement of receipt of Tender \nAn acknowledgement by or on behalf of the Principal or the Principal\'s Contact Person of \nreceipt of a Tender does not mean or imply that the Tender is a conforming Tender. \n7.2 \nInformation requests \n(a) \nAfter a Tender has been lodged, the Principal or the Principal\'s Contact Person may \nrequire a Tenderer to submit further information.  Tenderers must respond promptly \nto all such requests.  \n(b) \nAdditional information may be requested in any form required by the Principal.   \n(c) \nCompleted and resolved information requests will be taken to form part of the \nTender. However, any provision of additional information which is not in full \nconformance with the Tender Documents will have no force or effect unless the \nparticular provision is specifically noted as a departure from the Tender Documents. \n7.3 \nEvaluation  \nWithout in any way limiting the operation of clause 8:  \n(a) \nthe Principal may take into account in any evaluation of Tenders the information \nprovided by the Tenderer in response to each Tender Schedule and any other \nspecific evaluation criteria set out in this RFT and such other information obtained \nby the Principal in connection with the RFT process (including referee reports). The \nschedules or any specific evaluation criteria are not set out in any order and may \nnot be accorded equal weight by the Principal in its evaluation process; and \n(b) \nif: \n\n \n \n17 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \n(i) \nafter submission of its Tender, the Tenderer seeks any departure to the \nConditions of Contract that was not identified in its Tender, then the \nPrincipal may, in its absolute discretion, cease further engagement with \nthe Tenderer and revoke the Tenderer?s short-listed or successful status; \nand \n(ii) \nthe Tenderer seeks any departure that, in the Principal?s view, is \nextensive or material, then the Principal may, in its absolute discretion, \nexclude or refuse to further consider the Tender.  \n7.4 \nEvaluation criteria \nThe evaluation of Tenders will be based on (but not limited to) the criteria set out in the Tender \nParticulars (which are not listed in order of priority or importance).  \n7.5 \nDisclosure of Tender information \n(a) \nThe Principal?s public disclosure obligations are set out in the Government \nInformation (Public Access) Act 2009 (NSW), and the Tenderer acknowledges and \nagrees that any information provided as part of a Tender may be subject to \ndisclosure under that legislation. \n(b) \nWithout limiting clause 7.5(a), the Principal is at liberty to disclose any Tender \n(including an Alternative Tender or Non-Conforming Tender) and any other \ntendered information, to such persons as it considers necessary for the purpose of \nevaluating Tenders or obtaining advice, finance or approvals, for government \npurposes or as required by Law. \n(c) \nWhere any information or document is provided by a Tenderer on a confidential \nbasis or relates to a Tenderer?s trade secrets or confidential financial affairs, the \nTenderer should endorse the information or document accordingly and the Principal \nwill take that into account when deciding if and to what extent or on what conditions \nthe information might be disclosed to others. \n7.6 \nExchange of information between Authorities  \n(a) \nBy submitting a Tender, the Tenderer authorises the Principal to gather, monitor, \nassess, and communicate to other Authorities information about the Tenderer?s \nfinancial position and its performance in respect of any Contract awarded as a \nresult of this RFT process. Such information may be used by those Authorities in \nconsidering whether to offer the Tenderer future opportunities for work.  \n(b) \nThe Tenderer acknowledges that any information about the Tenderer from any \nsource, including reports of unsatisfactory performance may be taken into account \nby the Principal and other Authorities in considering whether to offer the Tenderer \nopportunities for NSW government work including evaluation of suitability for \nregistration, pre-qualification, selective tender lists, expressions of interest or the \naward of a contract.  \n(c) \nThe Tenderer acknowledges and agrees that the provision of the information by the \nPrincipal to any other Authority is a communication falling within section 30 of the \nDefamation Act 2005 (NSW). \n(d) \nThe Tenderer releases and indemnifies the Principal and all relevant Authorities \nfrom and against any Claim: \n(i) \nin respect of any matter arising out of the provision or receipt of such \ninformation; or \n\n \n \n18 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \n(ii) \nit might otherwise have for any loss to the Tenderer arising out of the \ncommunication of information including evaluation by any Authority or \nthe use of such information by a recipient. \n7.7 \nDue diligence \nWithout limiting any other provision in this RFT, by submitting a Tender, the Tenderer \nauthorises the Principal to undertake activities to verify that the information provided by the \nTenderer is accurate and that the Tenderer has the experience, capacity, and capability to \nperform the obligations of any Contract awarded as a result of this RFT process, including \nundertaking:  \n(a) \nindependent reference checking; and \n(b) \nindependent financial assessments.  \n8. \nNo contract and no obligation to consider or accept any tender \n8.1 \nNo Contract \n(a) \nThe Principal will notify a Tenderer if it is to be awarded a contract.   \n(b) \nSubject to clause 8.1(c), by submitting a Tender, the Tenderer acknowledges that: \n(i) \nno contract exists or will arise between the Principal and a Tenderer in \nrespect of the Project or the tender process unless and until a Contract is \nexecuted between the Principal and the Tenderer; and \n(ii) \nthe rights, powers and discretions given to the Principal and the \nPrincipal\'s Contact Person in these Conditions of Tendering are not \npursuant to any contract between the Principal or the Principal\'s Contact \nPerson and the Tenderer but rather are rights, powers and discretions \nthat the Principal and the Principal\'s Contact Person have as part of the \ntender process. \n(c) \nDespite clause 8.1(b), by submitting a Tender, a Tenderer is bound by the terms of \nthe Tender Form. \n8.2 \nNo obligation \n(a) \nWithout limiting a Tenderer\'s obligations under clauses 6 and 7, the Principal and \nthe Principal\'s Contact Person have no contractual or other legal obligation to a \nTenderer arising out of the invitation to submit a tender with respect to: \n(i) \nthe consideration, evaluation, acceptance or rejection of any Tender; or \n(ii) \nthe failure to consider, evaluate or accept any Tender.  \n(b) \nIn particular, the Principal and the Principal\'s Contact Person are under no \nobligation to: \n(i) \nreceive, consider, evaluate or negotiate any Tender; \n(ii) \nreceive, consider or evaluate any Tender in any particular way or within \nany particular time;  \n(iii) \naccept the lowest Tender or any Tender; or \n\n \n \n19 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \n(iv) \ngive any reasons for any decision they make in respect of the tender \nprocess. \n8.3 \nThe Principal not liable \n(a) \nWithout limiting clauses 8.2 or 12, to the extent permitted by Law, in no \ncircumstances will the Principal or the Principal\'s Contact Person or any of their \nrespective Personnel be liable to a Tenderer (whether a Tenderer is successful or \nunsuccessful) whether in contract, tort (including negligence or misrepresentation), \nunder statute (to the extent permitted by Law) or otherwise, for any costs, losses, \nexpenses, liabilities or damages incurred or suffered by any Tenderer: \n(i) \nin responding to the invitation to submit a tender, and in submitting any \nTender or in otherwise acting in reliance upon these Conditions of \nTendering; \n(ii) \narising out of or in connection with: \nA. \nany Tenderer\'s participation in or response to any Interactive \nProcess, discussions, negotiations, interviews, enquiries or \nrequests for details or information whether before or after the \nClosing Time; or \nB. \nany Tenderer\'s participation in the tender process generally; \nor \n(iii) \narising out of or in connection with the exercise, or failure to exercise, by \nthe Principal or the Principal\'s Contact Person of any of their rights, \npowers and discretions under these Conditions of Tendering, including \nrights under clause 8.4. \n(b) \nWithout limiting clause 8.3(a), any Tenderer that is not selected as the successful \nTenderer (including any Tenderer who has been selected as a preferred Tenderer \nor who the Principal has entered into negotiations with) will, subject to Law, have no \nclaim against the Principal or the Principal\'s Contact Person or their respective \nPersonnel, in relation to any decisions of the Principal or the Principal\'s Contact \nPerson: \n(i) \nto select another Tenderer as the successful Tenderer; \n(ii) \nto not select any of the Tenderers as the successful Tenderer; or \n(iii) \nto not proceed with the Project. \n8.4 \nDiscretions of the Principal \n(a) \nTo the extent permitted by Law, the Principal (either itself or through the Principal\'s \nContact Person) reserves the right in its absolute discretion, and without limiting \nany other rights which the Principal may have whether under these Conditions of \nTendering or otherwise, to do any one or more of the following without giving \nreasons: \n(i) \nwithdraw any invitation to tender; \n(ii) \namend these Conditions of Tendering, any other Tender Documents, or \nthe scope of the Project; \n(iii) \nvary, suspend or terminate the tender process; \n\n \n \n20 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \n(iv) \nextend the Closing Time; \n(v) \nchange the details for lodgement of Tenders;  \n(vi) \nreject or refuse to consider, evaluate or negotiate any Tender or all \nTenders;  \n(vii) \ndiscontinue consideration or negotiation of any Tender; \n(viii) \nterminate at any time the further participation in the tender process by \nany Tenderer; \n(ix) \ndecline to accept the lowest Tender or any Tender; \n(x) \naccept any Tender (whether a conforming Tender, Alternative Tender or \nNon-Conforming Tender); \n(xi) \nat any time, vary or alter any process or procedure regarding the \nconsideration or the evaluation of any Tender or Tenders (including the \ncriteria used for evaluation); \n(xii) \nadopt different approaches with different Tenderers; \n(xiii) \nrequire additional information, clarification or further offers from any one \nor more Tenderer (but is not obliged to take into account additional \ninformation provided);  \n(xiv) \nnegotiate on any aspect of a Tender before accepting or rejecting any \nTender and as part of this process, require one or more Tenderers to \nclarify, improve or consolidate any of the technical, commercial, legal, \nfinancial or operational aspects of their Tender;  \n(xv) \ninvite best and final offers from any one or more Tenderers; \n(xvi) \ninvite further or other persons to tender for the performance of the \nProject; \n(xvii) \nselect a Tenderer as a preferred Tenderer, or elect not to select any \nTenderer as a preferred Tenderer, or having selected a Tenderer as a \npreferred Tenderer, terminate that selection and select one or more \nother Tenderers as the preferred Tenderer(s), or negotiate with any \nTenderer notwithstanding it has not been selected as a preferred \nTenderer (and selection as a preferred Tenderer does not affect or limit \nthe Principal?s rights or the Tenderer?s obligations under this RFT and is \nnot a representation that a contract will be entered into between the \nPrincipal and that Tenderer); \n(xviii) \nnegotiate with one or more Tenderers and enter into the Contract without \nprior notice to any other Tenderer; \n(xix) \nnot proceed with the Project or the Contractor\'s Activities; \n(xx) \nproceed with the Project and the Contractor\'s Activities on the basis of a \ndifferent scope of work or on terms different from those stated in the \nTender Documents; \n(xxi) \nnegotiate with and enter into a contract with any person (including \nsomeone other than a Tenderer) for the performance of the Project and \nthe Contractor\'s Activities and/or any other work; \n\n \n \n21 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \n(xxii) \nconduct an Interactive Process or other discussions, with any one or \nmore Tenderers at any time during the tender process; \n(xxiii) \nissue Addenda or Information Documents; \n(xxiv) \nwaive any requirement or obligation under these Conditions of \nTendering;  \n(xxv) \npermit a Tenderer to change the identity of its participants; and \n(xxvi) \ntake such other action as it considers, in its absolute discretion, \nappropriate in relation to the tender process. \n(b) \nNo Tenderer is entitled to enquire into the basis of the Principal\'s decisions under \nclause 8.4(a). \n(c) \nTo the extent permitted by Law, Tenderers will have no claim against the Principal \nor the Principal\'s Contact Person arising out of the Principal\'s or the Principal\'s \nContact Person\'s exercise, or failure to exercise, any rights or discretions under this \nclause 8.4 or any other provision of these Conditions of Tendering.  \n8.5 \nRe-seller Model \nWithout limiting clause 8.4, the Tenderer acknowledges and agrees that if the Tenderer \nproposes to perform and/or complete the Project primarily through a Re-Seller Model, the \nPrincipal:  \n(a) \nwill not accept submission of the Tenderer?s own (or wholesale alternative) terms \nand conditions; \n(b) \nhas the right to take into account in any evaluation of Tenders the information \nprovided by the Tenderer in response to each Tender Schedule, which includes any \nadditional conditions that are proposed pursuant to this Tender Schedule;  \n(c) \nreserves the right in its absolute discretion to exclude or not progress the Tenders \nof Tenderers who propose to perform and/or complete the Project primarily through \na Re-seller Model; and \n(d) \nwhere two or more Tenderers are proposing to use the same third-party supplier\'s \nunderlying software or platform to perform and/or complete the Project (Platform), \nreserves the right to progress only one Tenderer?s Tender per Platform. \n9. \nFormal contract required \n(a) \nNo contract will come into existence unless and until the Principal and the \nsuccessful Tenderer enter into a Contract for the performance of the Project. \n(b) \nBefore any Contract is entered into, the Principal may require that a conformed \ncontract document be prepared that takes into account any changes to the Tender \nDocuments and the outcomes of any negotiations during the tender process. \n(c) \nEach Tenderer acknowledges that no other document issued and no other \nrepresentation made or conduct engaged in, by or on behalf of the Principal (other \nthan as set out in clause 9(a)) will be deemed to be acceptance of a Tenderer\'s \nTender or to create any contractual or other legal relationship between the Principal \nand a Tenderer or otherwise oblige the Principal to enter into a Contract with the \nTenderer. \n\n \n \n22 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \n10. \nDisclaimer \nEach Tenderer acknowledges that: \n(a) \nthe Information Documents have been provided to a Tenderer by the Principal for \nthe information only of the Tenderer; \n(b) \nan Information Document may be incorrect; \n(c) \nthe Principal requires each Tenderer to make its own enquiries to determine the \naccuracy and adequacy of any Information Document; \n(d) \nif the Principal has not prepared and is not the author of an Information Document, \nthe Principal does not adopt the Information Document and merely passes the \nInformation Document on to a Tenderer;  \n(e) \nneither the Principal or the Principal\'s Contact Person, nor any of their respective \nPersonnel, makes any representation that all information in the Principal\'s or the \nPrincipal\'s Contact Person\'s control or possession in relation to the Project has \nbeen provided to each Tenderer; and \n(f) \nneither the Principal or the Principal\'s Contact Person, nor any of their respective \nPersonnel, warrants, guarantees or makes any representation, or assumes any \nduty of care, or (to the extent permitted by Law) accepts any liability, with respect to \nthe completeness, accuracy, adequacy or correctness of: \n(i) \nthe Tender Documents; or \n(ii) \nany Information Document. \nNothing in this clause 10 limits the operation of the Process and Confidentiality Deed Poll (if \nany). \n11. \nTenderer?s warranty and acknowledgement \n11.1 \nTenderer?s warranty \nBy submitting a Tender: \n(a) \nthe Tenderer will be taken to represent and warrant that: \n(i) \nit has done all of the things mentioned in clause 3.1; \n(ii) \nit prepared its Tender based on its own investigations, interpretations, \ndeductions, information and determinations; \n(iii) \nit did not place any reliance upon the completeness, accuracy, adequacy \nor correctness of any of the documents, information or other things \nmentioned in clause 10; and \n(iv) \nits Tender is accurate and complies in all respects with the Tender \nDocuments and the requirements of all applicable Law;  \n(b) \nthe Tenderer will be taken to have acknowledged and agreed (to the extent \npermitted by Law) that neither the Principal or the Principal\'s Contact Person, nor \nany of their respective Personnel, has any liability to the Tenderer (whether in \ncontract, in tort, under statute (to the extent permitted by Law) or on any other \nbasis) with respect to or as a result of or arising from: \n\n \n \n23 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \n(i) \nany incompleteness or inadequacy of, or any inaccuracy or error in, or \nomission from; or \n(ii) \nany use of or reliance by the Tenderer upon, \nany of the Tender Documents, any Information Documents, information or any oral \ninformation provided; and \n(c) \nthe Tenderer will be taken to have read the Non-Returnable Schedules and to have \nconsidered them in submitting its Tender.  \n11.2 \nTenderer?s acknowledgement \nBy submitting a Tender, the Tenderer will also be taken to have acknowledged and agreed \nthat in considering its Tender and in entering into any Contract with the Tenderer, the Principal \nwill be relying upon the representations and warranties given by the Tenderer in the Tender \nForm and in these Conditions of Tendering. \n12. \nTenderer bears costs \n(a) \nAll costs and expenses incurred by a Tenderer in any way associated with the \ndevelopment, preparation and lodgement of its Tender, including costs of attending \nany Interactive Process, or providing any additional information required by the \nPrincipal, will be entirely borne by the Tenderer. \n(b) \nThe Principal is not liable for any costs, losses, liabilities, damages or expenses \nincurred by the Tenderer in preparing or lodging its Tender, or in respect of any \nInteractive Process, discussion, enquiries or negotiations undertaken with the \nTenderer following the lodgement of its Tender, even if the procurement process is \nterminated by the Principal.  In addition, the Principal is not liable to any Tenderer \nfor any costs on the basis of any promissory estoppel, quantum meruit or any other \ncontractual, quasi contractual or restitutionary grounds whatsoever as a \nconsequence of any matter or thing relating to, or incidental to the Tenderer?s \nparticipation in the RFT process. However, for clarity, nothing in this clause limits \nany rights that the Tenderer may have at Law.  \n13. \nGoverning law and jurisdiction \n(a) \nThese Conditions of Tendering and a Tenderer?s agreement to be bound by them, \nare governed by and are to be construed according to the Laws of New South \nWales. \n(b) \nEach Tenderer will irrevocably submit to the non-exclusive jurisdiction of the courts \nof New South Wales (and the courts to which appeals from those courts may be \nmade) with respect to matters arising under or in connection with these Conditions \nof Tendering and the Tenderer?s agreement to be bound by them. \n(c) \nEach Tenderer irrevocably waives any objection it may now or in the future have to \nthe venue of any proceedings in connection with these Conditions of Tendering and \nthe Tenderer?s agreement to be bound by them, and any claim it may now or in the \nfuture have that any such proceeding has been brought in an inconvenient forum, \nwhere that venue falls within clause 13(b). \n14. \nComplaints procedure \nTenderers may submit complaints in relation to this RFT (including in relation to any alleged \ncontravention of the EPP Direction) to:  \n\n \n \n24 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \n(a) \nthe Principal\'s Chief Procurement Officer by writing, addressed to: \nChief Procurement Officer \nDepartment of Customer Service \nMcKell Building, 2-24 Rawson Place \nSYDNEY NSW 2000. \n15. \nDefinitions and interpretation \n15.1 \nDefinitions \nIn these Conditions of Tendering, unless the context indicates otherwise, the following terms \nhave the meaning assigned to them below: \nAddendum means an addendum issued by the Principal or the Principal\'s Contact Person \nunder clause 2.4. \nAlternative Tender has the meaning given in clause 6.3(a). \nAuthority includes any governmental or semi-governmental or local government authority, \nadministrative or judicial body or tribunal, department, commission, public authority, agency, \nMinister, statutory corporation or instrumentality.  \nClaim means any action, suit, claim, demand, cause of action or notice, of any nature \nwhatsoever, at Law or in equity, including:  \n(a) \nin contract, whether for breach or for an entitlement under a contract;  \n(b) \nin tort for negligence or otherwise, including without limitation negligent \nmisrepresentation;  \n(c) \nfor contribution or indemnity at common law, equity or statute;  \n(d) \nfor restitution, unjust enrichment or quantum meruit;  \n(e) \nunder or for breach of statute; or \n(f) \nin any other way. \nClosing Time means the closing time and date identified in the Tender Particulars, or such \nlater closing time or date as the Principal or the Principal\'s Contact Person may notify in \nwriting. \nConditions of Contract means the Conditions of Contract identified in the Tender Particulars. \nConditions of Tendering has the meaning given in clause 2.1(a).  \nContract means a contract for the performance of the Project. \nContractor\'s Activities means all things or tasks which the "Contractor" is, or may be, \nrequired to do under the Contract. \nEPP Direction means Procurement Board Direction 2019-05 (Enforceable Procurement \nProvisions).  \n\n \n \n25 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \nInformation Document means any document, data or information (whatever its form including \nelectronic or oral) given to or made available to a Tenderer before the submission of Tenders \nor during the tender evaluation and negotiation period (including at any pre-tender briefing) in \nconnection with: \n(a) \nthis RFT; \n(b) \nthe Tender Documents; or \n(c) \nthe Project or the Contractor\'s Activities, \nother than the Tender Documents, including any document, data or information marked \n"information document", "for tenderer\'s information only", "for information only" or similar. \nInteractive Process has the meaning given in clause 3.3(a). \nLaw means the common law and any legislation of the Parliament of the Commonwealth of \nAustralia, of any State or Territory of the Commonwealth of Australia or of any other relevant \njurisdiction in force at any time and any rule, regulation, ordinance, by-law, statutory \ninstrument, order or notice at any time made under that legislation and, in each case, any \nconsolidations, amendments, re-enactments and replacement.  \nModern Slavery means: \n(a) \nany conduct that constitutes or would constitute a modern slavery offence, being an \noffense described in Schedule 2 of the Modern Slavery Act 2018 (NSW), or an \noffence of attempting or incitement to commit an offence described in Schedule 2 of \nthe Modern Slavery Act 2018 (NSW); \n(b) \nincludes any conduct that constitutes or would constitute an offence under any of \nthe Modern Slavery Laws as amended from time to time, including an offence of \nattempting or incitement to commit such an offence; and  \n(c) \nincludes conduct engaged in elsewhere than in New South Wales that, if it occurred \nin New South Wales, would constitute a modern slavery offence under paragraphs \n(a) or (b). \nModern Slavery Laws means: \n(a) \nthe Modern Slavery Act 2018 (Cth);  \n(b) \nthe Modern Slavery Act 2018 (NSW);  \n(c) \nDivisions 270 and 271 of the Commonwealth Criminal Code;  \n(d) \nsection 176(1A) of the Public Works and Procurement Act 1912 (NSW);  \n(e) \nsection 438ZE of the Local Government Act 1993 (NSW); and  \n(f) \nany other laws, regulations, codes and international conventions aimed at \ncombatting modern slavery, forced labour or human trafficking, from time to time in \nforce in or ratified by Australia and, where relevant, in or by other jurisdictions in \nwhich the parties operate, \neach as amended from time to time. \nNon-Conforming Tender has the meaning given in clause 6.2.  \nNon-Returnable Schedule means each document listed in Part 5 of this RFT. \n\n \n \n26 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \nPersonnel means:  \n(a) \nin respect of the Tenderer, any directors, officers, employees, consultants, agents \nand subcontractors of the Tenderer; and \n(b) \nin respect of the Principal, any directors, officers, employees, consultants, agents \nand contractors of the Principal (other than the Tenderer). \nPrincipal means the entity identified in the Tender Particulars.  \nPrincipal\'s Contact Person means the person identified as the Principal\'s Contact Person in \nthe Tender Particulars, or any other person from time to time appointed in writing by the \nPrincipal to be the Principal\'s Contact Person for the purposes of this RFT. \nProbity Advisor means the person or entity listed in the Tender Particulars (if any) or such \nother person notified by the Principal to Tenderers from time to time.  \nProcess and Confidentiality Deed Poll means the deed poll attached at Annexure B to these \nConditions of Tendering. \nProject means the goods, services or other activities which are to be the subject of the \nContract as described in general terms in the Tender Particulars (and more particularly \ndescribed in the Tender Documents). \nReasonable steps means those steps that are reasonable in the circumstances to prevent, \nidentify, mitigate and remedy modern slavery. In assessing whether steps are reasonable, the \nparties may refer to the NSW Anti-slavery Commissioner?s Guidance on Reasonable Steps \nand related information and resources published by the Commissioner. \nRe-seller Model means a model that utilises a third-party supplier\'s product (underlying \nsoftware or platform). \nRequest for Tender or RFT means this Request for Tender. \nSME & Regional Procurement Policy means the New South Wales Government Small and \nMedium Enterprise and Regional Procurement Policy (July 2021) a copy of which is available \nat https://buy.nsw.gov.au/. \nState Owned Corporation has the meaning given in the State Owned Corporations Act 1989 \n(NSW). \nStatement of Work means the statement of work, specifications, drawings and any other \ntechnical documents in Part 6 of this RFT.  \nTender means any tender lodged in response to this RFT. \nTender Documents means the documents listed in clause 2.1 and any other document issued \nto a Tenderer by the Principal or the Principal\'s Contact Person after the issue of the Tender \nDocuments by way of an Addendum and expressly stated to be a Tender Document. \nTender Form means the tender form attached at Annexure C to these Conditions of \nTendering. \nTender Particulars means the particulars set out in 0 of this RFT. \nTender Schedules means the tender schedules set out in Part 3 of this RFT. \nTender Validity Period means the period specified in the Tender Particulars. \n\n \n \n27 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \nTenderer means a person invited to lodge a tender for the performance of the Project \ndescribed in the Tender Documents. \nTransaction Platform has the meaning given in clause 1.4. \n15.2 \nInterpretation \nIn these Conditions of Tendering: \n(a) \nheadings are for convenience only and do not affect interpretation, \nand unless the context indicates a contrary intention: \n(b) \nan obligation or liability assumed by, or a right conferred on, two or more persons \nbinds or benefits them jointly and severally; \n(c) \nif a word or phrase is given a defined meaning, any other part of speech or \ngrammatical form of that word or phrase has a corresponding meaning; \n(d) \na word importing the singular includes the plural (and vice versa), and a word \nindicating a gender includes every other gender; \n(e) \n"person" includes an individual, the estate of an individual, a corporation, a \nGovernment, an Authority, an association or a joint venture (whether incorporated \nor unincorporated), a partnership and a trust; \n(f) \na reference to a party includes that party\'s executors, administrators, successors \nand permitted assigns, including persons taking by way of novation and in the case \nof a trustee, includes a substituted or an additional trustee; \n(g) \na reference to a clause, schedule or annexure is a reference to a clause, schedule \nor annexure in these Conditions of Tendering; \n(h) \na reference to a document (including the Tender Documents or any one of them) is \nto that document as varied, novated, ratified or replaced from time to time; \n(i) \na reference to a statute includes its delegated legislation and a reference to a \nstatute or delegated legislation or a provision of either includes consolidations, \namendments, re-enactments and replacements; \n(j) \n"includes" in any form is not a word of limitation; and \n(k) \na reference to "$" or "dollar" is to Australian currency or such other currency as \nspecified in the Tender Documents. \n \nAnnexure A ? Tender Particulars \nThe Tender Particulars are as follows: \nProject and Contract details \nPrincipal  \n(Clause 15.1) \nThe Department of Customer Service, for and on behalf of the Crown \nin right of the State of New South Wales \nABN: 81 913 830 179 \nAddress: McKell Building, 2-4 Rawson Place, Haymarket, NSW 2000 \n\n \n \n28 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \nProject \n(Clause 15.1) \nEstablishment of supply arrangements for mobile devices and \naccessories for Department of Customer Service (DCS). \n \nBackground and key \npriorities  \n(Clause 1.2) \nMobile devices and accessories are critical to enabling a connected, \nagile and productive workforce. \nThe purpose of this RFT is to engage one or more suppliers to \nprovide contemporary devices, accessories and associated services \nthat support DCS?s business and operational needs. \nKey priorities include product availability, competitive pricing, \ncustomer experience, supply continuity, and the provision of effective \nlifecycle services. \n \nConditions of Contract \n(Clause 15.1) \nThe Conditions of Contract will be those contained in the ICT \nAgreement (ICTA), as set out in Part 4 of this RFT. \n \nDoes this RFT relate to ICT \ngoods or services?  \n(Clause 1.5) \nYes  \nProbity Advisor \n(Clause 1.8 and 15.1) \nDoes clause 1.8 apply?  \nNo \nDoes the EPP Direction \napply to this RFT?  \n(Clause 3.4(b)) \nThe EPP Direction applies to this RFT.  \n \nPre-Tender \nIs a Process and \nConfideniality Deed Poll \nrequired? \n(Clause 1.6) \nNo \n \nWill there be a pre-tender \nbriefing? \n(Clause 3.2) \nNo \nPre-tender briefing details \n(Clause 3.2) \nNot applicable. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n29 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \nOther key dates \n(Clause 3.2) \nThe following dates are indicative only and subject to change at \nDCS\'s discretion. \nMilestones \nDate \nLast date for clarification \nquestions \nFriday, 25 September 2026 \nEvaluation Period \nOctober 2026 to November \n2026 \nNegotiations \nDecember 2026 to January \n2027 \nContract Award \nEarly February 2027 \n \nLodgement details \nClosing Time \n(Clause 15.1) \nClosing time: \n3:00pm (Australian Eastern Standard Time or \nAustralian Eastern Daylight Savings Time where \napplicable) \nClosing date: \nThursday, 15 October 2026 \nEvaluation \nTender Validity Period  \n(Clause  5(a) and 15.1) \n6 months from the Closing Time \nEvaluation criteria \n(Clause 7.4)  \nMandatory Criteria:  \nThe mandatory criteria are not point scored and each is assessed as \nPass or Fail. A Tenderer that fails any of the stated mandatory criteria \nwill be excluded from further consideration. \nThe mandatory criteria for this RFT are listed below: \nMC 1 \nICT Services Scheme (SCM0020) registration or \nevidence of application \nThe Tenderer must: \n? be prequalified as an advanced supplier under \nSCM0020/Category G01; or \n? have applied for prequalification under \nSCM0020/Category G01 and provide evidence of \nthat application with its Tender. \nTenderers not prequalified at the Closing Time must \nbecome prequalified under SCM0020/Category G01 \nbefore contract award. \nMC 2 \nModern Slavery Tender Schedule \nThe Tenderer must submit a completed Modern Slavery \nTender Schedule and be compliant. \nMC 3 \nSupplier Code of Conduct Acknowledgement and \nAnnual Compliance Commitment \n\n \n \n30 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \nThe Tenderer must: \n? submit a completed NSW Government Supplier \nCode of Conduct acknowledgement; \n? confirm compliance with the NSW Government \nSupplier Code of Conduct throughout the Contract \nTerm; and \n? agree to provide an updated acknowledgement \nannually, and on request by the Principal, during \nthe Contract Term. \nMC 4 \nConflict of Interest Declaration \nThe Tenderer must disclose any actual, perceived or \npotential conflicts of interest and, where a conflict exists, \nprovide details of the proposed management approach. \nMC 5 \nFinancial Viability Declaration \nThe Tenderer must declare that it: \n? is not insolvent or subject to any form of external \nadministration; \n? is financially viable and capable of supplying the \nGoods & Services; \n? has no current circumstances that may materially \naffect its ability to supply the Goods & Services; \nand \n? agrees to provide further financial information to \nthe Principal upon request for the purposes of due \ndiligence. \nMC 6 \nContract Conditions \nThe Tenderer must either: \n? confirm acceptance of ICT Agreement (ICTA); or \n? clearly identify and submit all proposed \ndepartures from the ICT Agreement (ICTA). \nFailure to identify departures in the Tender may result in \nthose departures not being considered during contract \nnegotiations. \n \nGeneral Criteria:  \nThe general criteria are scored by the Evaluation Committee and are \nlisted below: \nGC 1 \nProduct Suitability and Technical Compliance (8%) \nAssessment of the extent to which the proposed Goods: \n? are fit for purpose and meet the Principal\'s \nrequirements; \n? comply with the specifications set out in the \nStatement of Work; \n\n \n \n31 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \n? are compatible with the Customer\'s technology \nenvironment, including Apple Business Manager \n(ABM) and Samsung Knox; \n? provide appropriate security and connectivity \nfeatures; and \n? offer value-added functionality that enhances \nusability, performance or user experience. \nGC 2 \nSupply & Delivery Capability (16%) \nAssessment of the Tenderer\'s capability for the supply \nand delivery of the Goods and Services, including: \n? order management, fulfilment and delivery \nprocesses; \n? ability to meet agreed delivery timeframes and \nservice commitments; \n? stock management and approach to maintaining \nproduct availability; \n? management of supply constraints, product \ndiscontinuations and model refreshes; and \n? contingency arrangements to minimize disruption \nand ensure continuity of supply. \nGC 3 \nWarranty and Support Services (4%) \nAssessment of the Tenderer\'s capability to provide \nwarranty and support services, including: \n? warranty coverage and service inclusions; \n? repair, replacement and returns arrangements; \n? customer support and service request \nmanagement processes; \n? escalation and resolution procedures for service \nissues; and \n? ability to meet warranty and support service \ntimeframes. \nGC 4 \nGC 4: Service Delivery and Account Management \n(4%) \nAssessment of the Tenderer\'s approach to service \ndelivery and account management, including: \n? customer service and account management \narrangements; \n? communication, escalation and issue resolution \nprocesses; \n? management of service performance and \ncompliance with service levels; \n? approach to continuous improvement and \ncustomer satisfaction; and \n? governance, reporting and engagement \narrangements with the Principal. \n\n \n \n32 \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories | GSHS/9477  \n \nDepartment of Customer Service Standard Form - Request for Tender ? version 1.0 ? October 2024 \nGC 5 \nSME Participation (4%) \nAssessment of how the Tenderer will contribute to SME \nparticipation and local economic outcomes. \nGC 6 \nSustainability Commitment (4%) \nAssessment of Tenderer?s environmental, social and \neconomic sustainability outcomes. \n \nThe general evaluation criteria for this RFT that relate to price \nwill account for 60% of the total evaluation score. The evaluation \ncriteria for this RFT that do not relate to price will account for \n40% of the total evaluation score. \n \nContact details \nClient Support Centre  \n(Clause 4.2(e)(i)) \nClause 4.2(e)(i) applies: Yes   \nIf yes, the contact details for the Client Support Centre are as follows:  \nEntity:                NSW Procurement Service Centre \nTelephone: \n1800 679 289 \nEmail:  \nnswbuy@treasury.nsw.gov.au \nEmail address for submitting \ncomplaints \n(Clause 14(a)) \nEmail:  \ndcsprocurement@customerservice.nsw.gov.au \nChief Procurement Officer \nDepartment of Customer Service \nMcKell Building, 2-24 Rawson Place \nHaymarket, NSW 2000. \n \nPrincipal\'s Contact Person \n(Clause 15.1) \nName: \nShahana Ferdous \nEmail:  \nShahana.Ferdous@customerservice.nsw.gov.au \n \n\n'}, {'file_name': 'GSHS9477--Part-A-Request-for-Tender-Conditions.txt', 'extracted_text': ' \n  Version: 1.0 \n \nDate: October 2024 \n \n \n \nRequest for tender \nPart A - Conditions of Tendering \nRFT Title:  \n \nProvision of Mobile Devices and Accessories \nRFT Number: \n \nGSHS/9477 \n \nRFT issue date: \n \nThursday, 17 September 2026 \nRFT closing date: \n \nThursday, 15 October 2026 \nRFT closing time: \n \n3pm AEST and/or AEDT \nQuotation validity period: \n6 months \nContact officer: \n \nShahana Ferdous \